% The site variant of lemma_captured.fspy: argQ demands P as an
% obligation site instead of proving a lemma, and argP2 is a second,
% refuted derivation of P (from a presumption of R, which killR refutes).
%
% The same document graph up to the name of P's second derivation, the
% same labels (P, Q IN; R[t] OUT), and the same terms up to that name:
% what the exposure of a lemma does, a site did already.  In particular
% `evaluate argP.` is an exception on both: argP on top of P's stack,
% its supporter argQ captures P as the stack below argP - argP2 alone,
% which is OUT - while the labels have argQ IN through argP (tasks.org,
% aida-entrypoint-capture-adequacy).
lk.
declare P,Q,R:bool.
declare rp:(R->P).
declare pq:(P->Q).
declare qp:(Q->P).
declare nR:(~R).

argument argP : (P).
cut (Q->P) th.
axiom qp.
elim.
by default.
next.
axiom.
dixi.

argument argQ : (Q).
cut (P->Q) th.
axiom pq.
elim.
next.
axiom.
dixi.

argument argP2 : (P).
cut (R->P) th2.
axiom rp.
elim.
by default.
next.
axiom.
dixi.

counterargument killR : (R).
cut (~R) x.
axiom nR.
elim.
axiom.
dixi.

evaluate issue :P.
evaluate argQ.
evaluate argP.
